# Dunia Emosi — exclude non-served / dev-only weight from Vercel deploys.
# These are NOT referenced by any served page; keeping them out of the deploy
# bundle cuts ~475 MB (source art scratch + QA screenshots + tooling).

# Source-art scratch + AI-generation inputs (never served)
prompt/
Documents/

# DO NOT re-add `Sounds/` here. It was excluded with the note "never served",
# which was simply wrong, and it cost 3160 audio files on Vercel:
#   * Root Sounds/ IS runtime content -- game.js loads every Pokemon attack
#     sound from it, games/train-bgm.js takes its default + Thomas tracks from
#     it, and mobil.html / monster-candy.html / selamatkan-kereta.html point
#     <audio> straight at it. That is 2841 files.
#   * The pattern has NO leading slash, so gitignore semantics match a folder of
#     that name at ANY depth -- and Vercel matches case-insensitively. So it also
#     swallowed every lowercase games/film/*/sounds/ directory: 319 more files,
#     across 7 film games. thomas-look-out lost res/sounds/en/base64/mp3.js,
#     which its Cocos2d boot list loads as a SCRIPT, so that game died outright.
# Symptom on the tablet: "banyak berkas tidak bisa di download" -- the offline
# installer retried forever because those files always 404'd. GitHub Pages was
# unaffected the whole time, which is why this hid for so long.
# If deploy weight ever needs trimming, exclude a specific path with a LEADING
# SLASH and verify against the runtime, e.g. /Documents/, never a bare name.

# Dev tooling + QA artifacts (never served)
tools/qa-screenshots/
tools/*.mjs
tools/*.py
node_modules/

# Agent / editor / VCS scaffolding
.claude/
.git/
.github/

# Planning + docs that are not part of the runtime app
documentation and standarization/
"documentation and standarization"/
